{
  "about": "The world's textures (task 082): what tools/textures.mjs makes, and how. None is a photograph (the owner's rule, 2026-10-23): each is drawn by a generator in tools/made.mjs (generator, with its params), seamless, and its mean colour and contrast (match: the mean sRGB colour, and the spread of its luminance in sRGB's bytes) matched to what its references measure (ref: a Poly Haven texture, CC0, by its id, polyhaven, kept as a reference only, its file and its leaves' alpha where it has them, the green leaves only where green, greyed and lifted as tone says; or a reference photo of Braga, photo, refs/photos.json's, in its box of pixels), which node tools/textures.mjs --measure reads off them. A surface is a kind of ground (task 016), the one a game tiles over the ground tools/cover.mjs classes as that kind (ground), metres a side. A tree's bark and leaves (task 019) are a kind of tree's (tree): its bark metres a side, to wrap round its trunk; its leaves a spray of leaves drawn from their shape (leaf: shape, ovate, lanceolate, deltoid, cordate, rhombic, palmate, leaflet or needles; tones, the two across a leaf, before matching; teeth along its edge, veins either side of its midrib, how much of it is stalk, how far it curves; for needles, how many, the angles they spread at from the twig, their length as a share of the leaf's, their width), laid along twigs as spray says (branches, leaves to a branch per, fill more scattered over them, their length len as a share of the card, the angle they spread from the twig in degrees, droop, stretch and thin, the twig's colour or none; or a palm's frond).",
